  "key": "kc1",
  "qs": [
   {
    "q": "What does the Manager Multiplier Effect describe?",
    "opts": [
     "Managers doing more of the work themselves",
     "Coaching one person well, and the whole team gaining from it",
     "Managers needing more training than their teams",
     "Coaching everyone on the team the same way"
    ],
    "correct": 1,
    "fb": "Coach one person well, and the team gains.",
    "why": "When you coach one person well, their better work and engagement carry across the team, the way Kim's pitch won the contract for everyone.",
    "vo": "pc_n_1_20_q0",
    "wvo": "pc_n_1_20_w0"
   },
   {
    "q": "Why does leading yourself come before leading others?",
    "opts": [
     "Your team takes its steadiness from you",
     "It is faster to change yourself than others",
     "Your manager will check on it",
     "It keeps coaching conversations short"
    ],
    "correct": 0,
    "fb": "Your team takes its steadiness from you.",
    "why": "Melissa's own story makes the point. When she was running on empty, her team felt it. Looking after your own energy is what lets you be the anchor.",
    "vo": "pc_n_1_20_q1",
    "wvo": "pc_n_1_20_w1"
   },
   {
    "q": "In the Starting Line, your Athleader says, \"I'm not sure what I want from this yet.\" What's the best next move?",
    "opts": [
     "Suggest three goals they could choose from",
     "Move on to scheduling the check-ins",
     "Ask what would make the season worth it for them, then wait",
     "Tell them to come back when they know"
    ],
    "correct": 2,
    "fb": "Ask an open question, then wait.",
    "why": "An open question with no wrong answer, followed by a real pause, makes it safe for them to find their own goal. Suggesting goals hands them yours.",
    "vo": "pc_n_1_20_q2",
    "wvo": "pc_n_1_20_w2"
   },
   {
    "q": "What should every Starting Line end with?",
    "opts": [
     "A written performance goal",
     "A recurring 15-minute check-in on both calendars",
     "A list of the drills to complete",
     "A date for the next review"
    ],
    "correct": 1,
    "fb": "A recurring check-in, booked.",
    "why": "The rhythm is what carries the season. Book the fifteen-minute check-in before you leave the room, and the rest of the lessons have somewhere to land.",
    "vo": "pc_n_1_20_q3",
    "wvo": "pc_n_1_20_w3"
   }
  ],
